course: dictionary
lesson: 13475
title: Hypnosis: a deeply relaxed state
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hypnosis is a deeply relaxed, dreamlike state. Context helps you understand it. «Under hypnosis, Mia felt calm and sleepy, as if her worries were far away.» The words calm, sleepy and far away are clues. They tell you hypnosis makes a person feel relaxed and dreamy.
explain: «The therapist used hypnosis to help Sam feel less scared of the dentist.» Here the clues are therapist, help and less scared. A therapist is someone who helps people with their feelings or habits, so hypnosis is a way to help someone relax.
explain: Hypnosis can also be the act of putting someone into this state. In a cartoon, a magician might swing a shiny watch and make someone cluck like a chicken. Clues like «swinging watch» and «spinning eyes» show this is pretend, because real hypnosis is not shown with silly tricks like that.
explain: Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does «Mia felt calm and dreamy» make sense? Yes, so you know hypnosis here means a deeply relaxed, dreamlike state.
fact: Hypnosis is a deeply relaxed, dreamlike state in which a person focuses closely.
fact: Hypnosis can also mean the act of putting someone into this state.
fact: Some therapists use hypnosis to help people relax, stop bad habits or feel less scared.
fact: In cartoons and stories, hypnosis is shown with swinging watches and spinning eyes, but this is fiction.
fact: Stage hypnosis shows are entertainment, made to make the audience laugh and wonder.
exercise: «Under hypnosis, Mia felt calm and sleepy, as if her worries were far away.» What is hypnosis most like here? | A fast race to the finish | A cold winter storm | *A deeply relaxed, dreamlike state | A loud and busy party
exercise: «The therapist used hypnosis to help Sam feel less scared of the dentist.» Why did the therapist use hypnosis? | *To help Sam relax and feel less scared | To prove that cartoons are real | To make Sam lose his voice | To sell Sam a shiny watch
exercise: Lily says the magician in the cartoon swung a watch and made a man cluck like a chicken. Is this real hypnosis? | Yes, but only at the dentist | *No, this is fiction, made up for stories | No, because cartoons are never funny | Yes, all hypnosis works exactly like this
test: «The stage hypnosis show made the whole audience laugh.» What is stage hypnosis? | A medicine for headaches | A type of school test | A kind of swimming race | *Entertainment, a show to make people laugh
test: What does «under hypnosis» mean? | Sitting up in bed at night reading a book | Wearing a heavy winter coat | Running very fast around the track | *In a deeply relaxed, dreamlike state
exam: Which sentence uses the word hypnosis correctly? | «She ate a hypnosis for lunch.» | «The hypnosis raced across the football pitch.» | «The hypnosis was a red bicycle with two wheels.» | *«The therapist used hypnosis to help the boy feel calm.»
